hadiths[14]{hadithnumber,text}:
"129","

Mohammed bin Salam narrated to us, saying: 'Abdah informed us, from 'Ubayd Allah, from Sa'id bin Abi Sa'id, from Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of Allah was asked: ""Which people are the most honored?"" He said: ""The most honored of them with Allah are those whom He has purified."" They said: ""We are not asking about this."" He said: ""Then the most honored of people are Yusuf, the Prophet of Allah, the son of the Prophet of Allah, the son of the Friend of Allah."" They said: ""We are not asking about this."" He said: ""Then ask me about the noble ones of the Arabs in the time of ignorance and in Islam, when they have believed."""
"130","Mundhir at-Tawri reported what Muhammad ibn 'Ali (ibn al-Hanafiyya)\nsaid about, \Is the repayment of kindness anything except kindness?\"" He said"
"131","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, said, \The person who strives on behalf of the widows and poor\nis like those who strive in the way of Allah and like those who fast in the\nday and pray at night.\"""""
"132","'A'isha said, \A woman came to me who had two of her daughters with\nher. She asked me for something"
"133","Umm Sa'id bint Murra al-Fihri related from her father that the Prophet,\nmay Allah bless him and grant him peace, said, \I and the guardian of an\norphan will be in the Garden like these two.\"" (His two fingers)"""
"134","Al-Hasan reported that an orphan used to eat with Ibn 'Umar. One day\nhe called for food and looked for this orphan but could not find him. He\narrived after Ibn 'Umar had finished. Ibn 'Umar called for more food to be\nbrought to him but they did not have any. So he was brought sawiq and honey.\nHe said, \Here"
"135","Sahl ibn Sa'd reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, said, \I and the guardian of the orphan will be in the Garden\nlike that"
"136","Abu Bakr ibn Hafs reported that 'Abdullah would not eat unless an orphan\nwas at his table."
"137","Abu Hurayra reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him\nand grant him peace, said, \The best house among the Muslims is the house\nin which orphans are well treated. The worst house among the Muslims is the\nhouse in which orphans are ill treated. I and the guardian of the orphan\nwill be in the Garden like that"
"138","how ugly is misguidance after guidance! When you make a promise to your friend,\nfulfil your promise. If you do not, it will bring about enmity between you\nand him. Seek refuge in Allah from a companion who, when you mention something\nto him, does not help you and who does not remind you when you forget.\""139"""
"139","Najih Abu Umara said: I heard Al-Hasan say: I knew the Muslims, and a man among them would wake up and say: ""O my family, O my family, your orphan, your orphan. O my family, O my family, your poor, your poor. O my family, O my family, your neighbor, your neighbor."" And the best of you were hastened away while you are every day becoming more degraded. And I heard him say: ""And if you wished, you would see him a sinner plunging with thirty thousand into the Fire — may Allah fight him! He sold his share from Allah for the price of a goat. And if you wished, you would see him neglectful, dust-covered in the path of Satan, with no admonisher from himself nor from the people."""
"140","Asma' bint 'Ubayd said, \I said to Ibn Sirin"
"141","'Awf ibn Malik reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, said, \I and a woman who is widowed and is patient with her child\nwill be like these two fingers in the Garden.\"""""
"142","Shumaysa al-'Atakiyya said, \The disciplining of orphans was mentioned\nin the presence of 'A'isha and she said"
